# Linear Triage (automation 2 of 2)

Read `.cursor/skills/linear-triage.md` before running. Runs ~1h after the curator pass and keeps the Linear board healthy — all **in Linear**, via the `LINEAR_API_KEY` (auth/helper/IDs in `docs/internal/ci-cd/CURSOR_AUTOMATIONS.md`).

Key points:
- **Main job — process the Triage inbox:** for each Triage item, dedup, set **Project**, set **Priority** (required to leave Triage), optionally set an estimate, add relations, then **promote** clearly-actionable work to **Backlog** so `/next` sees it.
- **Organize broadly, destroy narrowly:** setting project/priority/estimate/relations on any Triage item is fine; but Cancel / mark-duplicate / re-body only `suggestion`-owned issues (run the pre-write label gate). Never cancel or re-body a human-filed issue — leave it in Triage with a comment instead.
- **Don't auto-promote a real human decision** — surface it for a human; only auto-promote suggestion-owned or clearly well-formed items.
- **Light Backlog hygiene** (Pass B): fill missing priority / wrong project on `suggestion`-owned issues; flag obvious `stale`. Keep it small — hygiene, not a re-plan. Never restructure epics/Projects.
- **Read-only on code** — never edit files, open PRs, or create GitHub issues.
